==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[UltraBaaBaa]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Kid Tappa]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**3 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Using anti-zombie cats makes this stage a lot easier. Bringing [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] helps to defeat the Zoges and Znaches at the start of the level, and stacking them along with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] can help defeat the Dread Bore and Zories. Stack your Cadaver BearCats on the UltraBaaBaa while simultaneously spawning some meatshields and upgrading your wallet. When you have over 8k+ cash, spawn [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]] (or a different barrier breaker cat of your choice) and attack the base. When the Dread Bore burrows, use the Holy Blast cannon to make it resurface. The stack of Cadaver Bears should knockback the Dread Bore, while the Housewives perma slow the Zories and the knockbacked Dread Bore. Eventually, the Dread Bore will die from the Cadaver Bears and you will win.

If you have [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], you can stack a lot of them on UltraBaaBaa to completely destroy the stage with their powerful waves.

